WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.920
Netflix's The Witcher delivers on its promise
of high-fantasy monster hunting, but it's

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.300
not always easy to follow.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.740
If you made it to the end of the first season
and feel a little lost, you're not alone.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.940
Here's what you need to know.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.280
Even though "Much More," the final episode
of The Witcher's first season, is happening

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.660
in one more-or-less united timeline, our characters
don't cross paths until the very end.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.390
Ciri spends the bulk of the episode with a
kindly commoner who wants to adopt Ciri as

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:26.450
her daughter.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:30.660
Meanwhile, Geralt begins the episode in the
same refugee camp that Ciri visited in episode

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.180
two, where a local merchant is clearing out
dead bodies.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.570
Geralt defends the merchant from some zombie-like
monsters, but is wounded in the process.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.440
The merchant, who happens to be the commoner's
husband, puts Geralt on his cart and starts

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.060
towing him to safety.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:47.989
Yennefer, whose adventure takes up most of
the episode, makes a stand with other mages

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:51.330
at Sodden, where they fight to defend the
north from the Nilfgaardian [nilf-GARD-ee-in]

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.330
army.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.010
In the aftermath, Tissaia magically calls
out for Yennefer.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.860
Ciri hears her and heads to the woods, where
she meets Geralt for the first time.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.170
She asks the witcher who Yennefer is, but
before he can answer, the credits roll.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:09.460
Why, exactly, did Nilfgaard invade the north,
raze Cintra, and turn Sodden into a massacre?

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.250
It's after more than just Ciri.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.930
If you track Nilfgaard's history over The
Witcher's different timelines, you'll actually

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:19.330
see the story of a humiliated nation that
rises from the ashes in order to restore its

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:20.720
lost glory.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:24.080
Early on, before Yennefer's ascension, Nilfgaard
is a joke.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.990
Its king, Fergus, wastes the kingdom's money
on frivolous pursuits.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:32.060
The Brotherhood of Sorcerers hope that a court
mage can help bring Fergus under control.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:35.990
Instead, sometime around Geralt's story in
episode three, someone known as the Usurper

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:40.409
organizes a rebellion, overthrows Fergus,
and takes the crown.

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:44.560
Sometime after that, Fergus' son Emhyr reclaims
the Nilfgaardian throne and sends his army

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.630
out to conquer the north.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:50.770
That's when Cintra burns, and how Sodden becomes
the site of the mages' last stand.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:55.280
Amazingly, the mages manage to hold Sodden
until help arrives from one of the northern

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.280
kingdoms.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.750
You know that king who arrives, riding a white
horse with an army behind him?

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:04.259
That's King Foltest of Temeria, and if that
name sounds familiar, it should.

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:05.400
You've met him before.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.439
King Foltest is the same king Geralt met in
"Betrayer Moon."

00:02:08.439 --> 00:02:12.090
He's the one who slept with his sister, who
then died and gave birth to the striga that

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.540
Geralt had to fight.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:17.610
Foltest shows up thanks to Triss Merigold,
the mage assigned to his court, who fought

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.060
at the battle of Sodden.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.010
The king still owes Triss for helping Geralt
save his daughter.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:25.060
It's just too bad that he took his sweet time
getting there.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:28.230
"Much More" ends on a couple of cliffhangers.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:33.160
Ciri and Geralt meet for the first time and,
more importantly, Yennefer seems to have disappeared.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.800
After unleashing some major magic on the Nilfgaardian
army, Yennefer more or less vanishes.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.480
The last we hear of her, Tissaia is worriedly
calling out her name.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.790
Given that "Much More" clearly establishes
that using powerful magic can kill a person,

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:46.959
it's cause for alarm.

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:49.260
Still, don't worry too much.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:53.090
Yennefer is a major player in the books and
unless the show is planning to deviate pretty

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:57.290
radically from the source material, the sorceress
should pop up in season two.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.819
It might take a little while, but we're almost
certain she'll be there.

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:05.459
While Yennefer is defending the north from
Nilfgaard's advance, Geralt spends most of

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:09.600
the season finale laying in the back of a
hay cart, suffering poison-induced flashbacks

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.769
to his past.

00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:14.420
The biggest revelation to come out of those
visions is that Visenna, a sorceress, raised

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.850
Geralt when he was a small boy.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:20.350
In fact, while the show doesn't make it entirely
clear, Witcher lore dictates that Visenna

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.500
is Geralt's biological mother.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.940
Visenna didn't take care of Geralt for long,
though.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:28.489
When he was still young, she abandoned him,
leaving him to be taken to Kaer Morhen where

00:03:28.489 --> 00:03:30.430
Witchers live and are trained.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:34.230
In "Much More," Geralt comes face-to-face
with his mother for the first time in decades

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.459
in a scene that could be magic or just a hallucination.

00:03:37.459 --> 00:03:41.430
Whether Visenna actually came to visit Geralt
or not, you can expect more details about

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.330
the Witcher's childhood in season two.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.879
"Don't ask any more questions.

00:03:45.879 --> 00:03:49.260
The answers will only hurt us both.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:53.299
It's time to move on, Geralt."

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:57.019
The other major figure introduced in Geralt's
visions is Vesemir.

00:03:57.019 --> 00:04:01.430
After Visenna disappears, it's Vesemir who
comes to lil' Geralt's aid, and Geralt utters

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:04.659
his name a few times during his poison-induced
delirium.

00:04:04.659 --> 00:04:09.110
The Witcher doesn't explain who Vesemir is,
but fans of the franchise know him quite well.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:11.409
Like Geralt, Vesemir is a witcher.

00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:15.440
He lives at the witcher stronghold, Kaer Morhen,
and is one of the oldest and most respected

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.260
members of the fraternity.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:20.959
Thanks to a past adventure gone awry, Vesemir
rarely leaves Kaer Morhen.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:24.669
However, he's one of the best instructors
the witchers have, and he functions as a de

00:04:24.669 --> 00:04:27.509
facto father figure to Geralt in the books.

00:04:27.509 --> 00:04:31.460
The show will probably make a few changes
to the story, but the season finale has already

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.800
put the basic pieces in place.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:36.180
Expect Vesemir to pop up during season two.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:41.150
Ultimately, the first season of The Witcher
is about three people trying to find a family.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:44.490
We don't know it until the finale, but the
Geralt we meet at the beginning of the show

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.600
was abandoned by his mother.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.970
Yennefer is sold off by her foster father
and deprived of the ability to have children.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.900
Ciri's family is killed in the very first
episode.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.689
Each one of these characters has the opportunity
to find a new family over the course of the

00:04:57.689 --> 00:04:59.860
season, and each one rejects it.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.899
Instead, our three heroes find comfort in
each other.

00:05:02.899 --> 00:05:05.610
In the books, the trio form a makeshift family.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:10.039
The show isn't there quite yet, but if you're
paying attention, it's very clear where it's

00:05:10.039 --> 00:05:11.039
going.

